# 10. Spring Session and removed integrations

Spring Boot 4 removes some direct integrations that previously existed.

| Feature                  | Migration impact                    |
| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| Spring Session Hazelcast | Direct Boot support removed         |
| Spring Session MongoDB   | Direct Boot support removed         |
| Spring Session Redis     | Property namespace changed          |
| Reactive Pulsar          | Reactive auto-configuration removed |
| Spock integration        | Boot integration removed            |

For Hazelcast and MongoDB session implementations, you may still be able to use the respective ecosystem libraries independently, but you must manage their integration and compatibility yourself.

For reactive Pulsar, review whether the application can use the supported non-reactive integration or requires a different messaging architecture.

For Spock, check the Groovy 5 compatibility status of your testing stack before deciding on an alternative.

