# 14. Other important behavioural changes

These changes may not break compilation, but can change production behaviour.

| Area              | Change                                                                          | Potential impact                          |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Tracing           | `management.tracing.enabled` becomes `management.tracing.export.enabled`        | Tracing export configuration              |
| Actuator          | JSpecify nullability replaces old nullable declarations for endpoint parameters | Custom endpoint compatibility             |
| Static resources  | `/fonts/**` added to common static locations                                    | Spring Security resource matching         |
| Logging           | UTF-8 default charset                                                           | Log ingestion and parsing                 |
| Jackson           | All classpath modules automatically detected                                    | JSON output changes                       |
| Health            | Liveness/readiness groups enabled by default                                    | Kubernetes probes                         |
| DevTools          | LiveReload disabled by default                                                  | Developer workflow                        |
| Forwarded headers | WAR deployment behaviour changes                                                | Reverse-proxy URLs                        |
| HTTP clients      | JDK HTTP client uses virtual threads when enabled                               | Threading and performance characteristics |

One particularly interesting security detail is the addition of `/fonts/**` to common static resource locations.

If you use:

```
PathRequest.toStaticResources().atCommonLocations()
```

your security configuration may now match more resources than before.

If you do not want font resources included, explicitly exclude them:

```
PathRequest.toStaticResources()
    .atCommonLocations()
    .excluding(StaticResourceLocation.FONTS);
```

