## Final architectural assessment

The key insight is that Spring Boot 4 migration has three fundamentally different types of incompatibility:

| Type                          | Example                                | Can automation solve it?       |
| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Structural incompatibility    | Package rename, removed API            | Mostly yes                     |
| Configuration incompatibility | YAML property rename                   | Partially                      |
| Semantic incompatibility      | Security, retry, persistence behaviour | Requires functional validation |

I would design a migration factory around these three categories rather than simply collecting compilation errors and asking AI to fix them.

The most dangerous failures are not compilation failures. They are applications that compile, start successfully and silently behave differently in production.

That should be the central design principle for any Spring Boot 3-to-4 migration programme.
